d positive book value"},{"method":"Net current asset value (net-net)","why":"current assets less all liabilities is negative (−$1.71 a share): no net-net value — normal for a company funded by long-term debt"},{"method":"Earnings power value (EPV)","why":"needs a positive normalized operating margin and the WACC (not for banks or insurers)"},{"method":"FCFE DCF (cash to shareholders)","why":"needs the DCF, positive net income and positive equity"},{"method":"H-model dividend discount","why":"pays no dividend (or its cost of equity is within a point of the terminal growth)"},{"method":"Real option to expand","why":"only for loss-making or fast-growing (15%+) companies with a peer margin and a price history"},{"method":"EV/Sales fair multiple (multi-factor fit)","why":"only for non-financial companies with revenue ≥ $50M and the cross-company fit"}],"stage":{"key":"pre_revenue","label":"Pre-revenue","why":"revenue not reported over four quarters, operating income ≤ 0","rule":"revenue under $25M over four quarters and operating income ≤ 0 (a pipeline no filing prices)","weights":[["Net cash (floor)",0.5],["Tangible book (asset value)",0.3],["Survival-weighted value",0.2]]},"note":"Every figure above is from the company's SEC filings (XBRL frames, or the main site's reading of its 10-K/10-Q), the hub's daily prices, the debt module or the consensus module, as each line says; every assumption is fixed in the code before any result is seen. History and models, not investment advice."},"range":[0.0,55.7923]}